WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.201
Russian forces are

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.168
making gradual

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.069
gains as they try

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.772
to encircle Ukrainian fighters in Bakhmut

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:07.974
President Zelensky is calling it, quote,

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:09.843
one of the toughest battles yet

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:10.643
despite a Russian blitz,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:11.511
Ukrainian forces say

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.812
that they are still holding on

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.980
to a key highway

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.582
in the fiercely contested city.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:16.516
Just a short time ago.

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:16.883
The defense

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:18.251
secretary, Lloyd Austin,

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:20.787
said it would not be a strategic setback

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:22.522
if Ukrainians decide to reposition

00:00:22.522 --> 00:00:24.924
in some areas to the West of Bakhmut.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.459
The town's deputy mayor

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:27.460
telling CNN

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.329
there are about 4500

00:00:29.329 --> 00:00:31.531
Ukrainian residents still in the city

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.866
and in harm's way.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.334
So let's bring in now retired U.S.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.569
Army Major General Mike Lyons.

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.704
Good morning to you.

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:40.140
Let's focus on Bakhmut here.

00:00:40.173 --> 00:00:42.342
So the secretary is saying

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.376
that it would not be

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.512
a strategic setback for Ukraine

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:47.247
if they lose this city.

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:48.181
Is that true?

00:00:48.181 --> 00:00:50.050
And what does this the significance of?

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.151
Yeah, I think it is true.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.919
I think the bottom line is both sides

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:53.753
are using this battle

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:55.188
to grind the other side down.

00:00:55.188 --> 00:00:56.990
And Ukraine's winning in that regard.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.591
They're about a seven to one ratio

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.659
seven to one Russias down

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:00.460
for one Ukraine.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:02.562
However, they still don't have enough

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.830
manpower there.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:04.264
Here's really

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.398
what's happening on the ground right now.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:05.965
The Russians.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.666
From what we can tell,

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.068
are using a kind of envelopment

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.302
to try to envelop the city here,

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.204
a very kind of wide circle here.

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.406
Why hasn't Russia taken it directly?

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:14.374
And I'll tell you why.

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.208
There's a river.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:16.609
Ukraine has used an incredible

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:18.344
amount of obstacles

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.612
in order to protect the city.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.214
There's a river that goes here that

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:22.882
the Russians can't navigate at all.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.583
And so we can tell

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.118
what either side is doing by

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.986
how they drop bridges across rivers.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:27.587
So, for example,

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:28.354
the Ukraine military

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:29.689
just dropped that river,

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.924
which tells me now

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:31.925
they're retreating back

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:32.992
into the town of Buck Mode

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.294
and eventually taking this

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.395
this is the 504

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.798
the 504 road back to even, let's say.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.066
But the Russians now,

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.868
they drop a bridge here and come over.

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.536
So they're trying to prevent

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:44.671
the Ukrainians

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.840
from from escaping from this route

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:47.440
there as well.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.142
So we're seeing now

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.211
actually what both sides are going to do

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.246
and likely where Ukraine will be able

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.547
to evade Russian forces

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:55.348
to leave the city.

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.283
So considering what you just said

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.118
and how they're surrounded.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.319
How much longer do you think

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.753
Ukrainian forces can hold on?

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.455
So so they've got to decide

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.990
how much more casualties

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.891
they really want to take.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:05.692
And both sides

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:06.793
have been grinding each other down.

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:07.560
And here at this point,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.761
I think they're going to do this

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.163
for the next 24 to 48 hours.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:10.663
And there's no

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.532
there's no loss in that for them.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:12.866
You know,

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.901
they'd when the enemy is strong

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:15.468
or at this point,

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:16.603
I think that's really what

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:17.937
with the decision that they're making.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.272
Can we talk about the volunteer group

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.406
because they have been spearheading

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.808
this push for a path.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.942
Can you explain

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.644
to us their involvement here?

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:26.713
They're mercenaries about 50,000 troops

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.081
we know in the dumbass region.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:31.751
10,000 regular contractors about 40,000.

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:33.019
Penal colony prisoners

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.220
people that have

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:34.954
made this choice

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:36.089
to come join the battle here

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.123
because as opposed to sitting

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.558
in a Russian penal colony,

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:40.226
they're unbounded by the laws of land

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:40.793
and warfare.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:41.761
Russia uses them

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.062
for plausible deniability.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:46.166
They were first deployed back in 20 2014

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.334
and Crimea as the little green men.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.636
They're not really warriors.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:50.937
Their head for Goshen

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:54.274
is a former caterer of Vladimir Putin.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.141
But here's the deal

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.109
we now see that he's

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.178
now complaining about the situation

00:02:58.178 --> 00:02:59.078
and he says

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:00.180
they're not getting enough ammo.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.614
So he's now sensing a loss.

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:02.515
He's sensing

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.082
that they're not

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.050
going to be able to hold it.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:04.751
And really

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:05.985
what they've done to the city

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:06.986
the cities and rebels

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:07.387
and center

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:11.324
4500 left from what was 80,000 civilians.

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:12.225
There's nothing

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.293
that if they've really not gained

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.394
any victory.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.228
They're not bound by

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:16.329
sort of traditional rules.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.730
Is this why they're involved

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.299
instead of Russian troops?

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.301
They can't seem to muster enough

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:21.968
Russian troops

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:22.835
that want to do this fight.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.870
This is a suicide mission.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:24.103
Again,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.306
these frontal assaults here on

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.840
locations in trench warfare

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.676
with all the different obstacles.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:30.810
The Russian soldiers are smart.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.045
They recognize they're not going to

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.146
they're not going to

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.547
survive those battles.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.281
Thank you. Peter.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.983
Michael, good to see you.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:37.650
Thank you.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:38.318
Let's go straight

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:38.651
to CNN's

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:41.087
most about live for us in Kyiv right now.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.555
Hello to you, Melissa.

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.790
The fight has been going on

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.891
for more than seven months.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:45.425
Now, wondering

00:03:45.425 --> 00:03:47.594
if Ukraine will be able to turn it around

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.394
and keep the city

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.799
I think their aim, Don, is at this point

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.367
just to hold it for as long as they can.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.335
And this is their tried

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:56.603
and tested strategy.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:58.004
We've seen it in other towns

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:58.905
in this war so far,

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:00.807
although none at the heart of a battle

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.342
this long yet

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.443
to try and hold on

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:04.644
for as long as they can,

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.012
whatever the cost to them

00:04:06.012 --> 00:04:07.380
insofar as it wears down

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.314
the Russian ability

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.116
to continue waging this war

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.051
and whatever the cost

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.791
Ukrainian forces

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.261
giving all their can to defend Bakhmut

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.430
or what's left of it.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:26.065
After the longest battle of the war,

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:28.067
one of the oldest cities in the Donbass

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.103
lies in ruins.

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.239
There were no orders,

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.440
no decisions were made

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.476
regarding withdrawal from Bakhmut.

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.611
There have been no tactical changes.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.946
We are holding the defense

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.115
abandoned by more than

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.149
90% of

00:04:43.149 --> 00:04:44.050
its population

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.119
over the course of the seven month siege.

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:48.454
Only those who couldn't leave before

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.555
are left.

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:50.723
The intense fighting

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:51.090
means

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.592
that only five to ten people

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.927
a day can now be evacuated.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.430
Compared to the 500 to 600 a day

00:04:57.664 --> 00:04:58.865
when the evacuation

00:04:58.865 --> 00:05:00.700
started at the end of February,

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.735
according to the city's deputy mayor,

00:05:04.237 --> 00:05:06.372
the Russians throwing all they have at

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.909
the city, says the deputy mayor.

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:13.012
Heavy artillery, mortar fire, airstrikes

00:05:13.279 --> 00:05:14.947
and a substantial commitment

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.182
of ground forces,

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.583
both regular soldiers

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.652
and volunteer mercenaries.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:21.621
But Russian advances have come at huge

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:22.555
cost.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:23.289
Wave after

00:05:23.289 --> 00:05:23.823
wave of

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.024
Russian soldiers

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.493
have been sent to their deaths.

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.429
And Ukraine has accused Russia

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:31.464
of exaggerating its gains,

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:33.166
claiming they still control one of the

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.867
major highways into Bermuda.

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.404
A lifeline for Ukrainian defenders.

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.406
With one Ukrainian commander

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.542
tweeting that there are many ways still

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.344
to get into the city.

00:05:44.344 --> 00:05:45.712
Analysts have questioned

00:05:45.712 --> 00:05:48.114
the strategic importance of Bermuda.

00:05:48.114 --> 00:05:49.382
But that has not stopped

00:05:49.382 --> 00:05:51.284
Moscow's intense campaign

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.553
to capture the city.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.756
Nor Ukraine's existential fight

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:58.224
to keep it.

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.760
The unceasing barrage of artillery fire

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:02.962
hasn't just killed or forced out

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.697
most of the city's civilians.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.366
It's taken a huge toll

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:08.501
on Ukrainian soldiers, too.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.669
As the battle turns

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:13.473
to close quarters, street fighting

00:06:14.107 --> 00:06:15.508
But Ukraine continues

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.143
its fierce fight for victory.

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.444
Even as Russian forces

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.946
continue to close in

00:06:19.946 --> 00:06:20.680
on a city

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.014
that's already a byword

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.583
for Ukrainian resilience,

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.351
On the battlefield

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:28.688
what's most remarkable,

00:06:28.688 --> 00:06:29.355
maybe, Dawn,

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.023
is that more than 100 years

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:32.558
after the end of World War One,

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:34.260
just how much this looks like

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:36.362
some of the early battles of that war.

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:37.630
Trench warfare,

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:38.431
heavy artillery

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.365
and wave after

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:41.334
wave of inexperienced soldiers

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:42.635
on both sides

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:43.936
being sent to their certain death.

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:45.772
And it's happening in Europe again.

